      "prefLabel": "Administrator",
      "title": "Administrator",
      "notation": "administrator",
      "definition": "Administers the role graph itself: who exists, what they may act as, and what they may do. The ONE lane whose activities change the substrate every other diagram's lanes bind to — which is why it is drawn rather than left as a filesystem edit. Declared 2026-09-20 on the owner's answer that administration is a swimlane; `role-model.md`'s rule is that a role is never invented to make a diagram drawable, so it waited for that.",
