      "label": "Authoring agent",
      "scopeNote": "Runs every stage up to the edge of authorisation — brief, declare, measure, move-and-remeasure, isolate — and Task_Propose is the last thing it does off its own judgement: reporting sizes and what would break, then waiting. Verification here is always by RE-RUNNING the measurement rather than by an assignment being locally reasonable, which is why Task_Move loops back to Task_Measure and not to the gate — a move that looks right is not yet a move that measured right.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/kg/graph-detanglement.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_KgSeparation/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_KgSeparation",
      "label": "Authoring agent",
      "scopeNote": "Briefs, measures the signals, runs declare-detangle-isolate, reports what would move, seeds the repositories once they exist, and adopts each later release. Verification is always by re-running a gate, never by a change looking right.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/kg/kg-separation.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MethodologyFromSource/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_MethodologyFromSource",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Does every step between the share and the review, and records each decision it made with its reason, so the owner reviews a record rather than an impression.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/library/methodology-from-source.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_Translation/Lane_Platform",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_Translation",
      "label": "Agent / platform (automated)",
      "scopeNote": "Everything in this process that runs without asking: extraction to a template, injection of a catalogue, the staleness comparison, and writing the official rendering once sign-off exists. It decides nothing a person would disagree about — every branch it takes is computed from a hash or a file's presence.\n\nIt is one lane rather than two because agentic and mechanical is a judgement rather than a line (see the role model), and nothing in THIS process turns on which of the two ran a step. Where that distinction does matter, the process says so by putting the step in the reviewer's lane instead.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/library/translation-workflow.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Close/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_CRDM_Close",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Holds no judgement in this diagram: both prior lanes already decided — sign-off, then confirmation against criteria — so this lane's only accountability is executing the close exactly when authorised and never before, on an issue that is the stakeholder's record rather than the agent's to close on its own reading of the thread.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_DataModel/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_CRDM_DataModel",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Does the actual modelling — entities, relations, and the declaration that makes the model machine-readable rather than prose — and absorbs the entire cost of a revise: the gate loops back to A_Entities whichever confirmation failed, BA's or the stakeholders', so this lane cannot assume a cardinality objection leaves its entities untouched.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-data-model.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Deliver/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_CRDM_Deliver",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Every loop-back in this phase — a rejected increment, an MVP not ready, stakeholder feedback — lands on A_Implement rather than on Call_OptionsAnalysis, so this lane always reworks an approach already chosen and never re-selects one. Deciding that the APPROACH itself is wrong is not this lane's call: that belongs to the calling step in crdm-requirements.bpmn, one level up.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-deliver.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Issue/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_CRDM_Issue",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "The only CRDM sub-diagram in this slice where the BA has no lane of its own: A_AskCreate is still an Agent-lane activity, so the permission this process exists to enforce is obtained out of band rather than modelled as a cross-lane handoff, unlike crdm-requirements-definition.bpmn and crdm-close.bpmn elsewhere in the same methodology.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-issue-linking.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Needs/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_CRDM_Needs",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Drafts the needs statement but never decides it is right — A_Synthesise is the sole target when GW_Needs loops back — and this process's own documentation calls an unconfirmed synthesis \"an agent's summary, not a requirement,\" which is exactly what this lane alone produces before the two lanes below it look at it.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-needs.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Requirements/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_CRDM_Requirements",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Owns Phases 2 through 4a end to end, but the revise loop (GW_Reqs' 'revise' branch) re-enters at A_DefineReqs rather than back at A_MapWorkflow — so mapping the current workflow is this lane's one-time fact-finding, done once per phase run, while defining requirements and comparing options is what gets redone against BA feedback until Lane_Stakeholders approves.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-requirements-definition.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_CRDM",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Holds the one gate whose \"no\" branch ends the entire process rather than routing into a child — GW_Feature's own documentation: a subprocess would have to re-ask the same question to route on the answer. From there it carries the BA's need through all six phases as a straight chain of subprocess calls, with no branching of its own.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-requirements.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Signoff/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_CRDM_Signoff",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Turns Lane_BA's two decisions into durable artefacts: A_CreateBeans and A_RecordKg each mint their own bean directly with the CLI, since the engine's own vocabulary has no create, only claim, note and resolve on an instance's bean. A_AnnounceBranch then closes the phase on its one path to End with no loop of its own, so it fires exactly once — Phase 6's own loops re-enter implementation on the same branch without ever crossing back through this edge.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-signoff.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SessionStateMachine/Lane_Machine",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_SessionStateMachine",
      "label": "Agent (playing the machine)",
      "scopeNote": "Classifies every turn into exactly one of three effects at Gateway_TurnEffect — nothing changed, state changed, ending — a fresh judgement each time because a table cannot key on intent and a wrong read is corrected by the next turn. It records that a bean was claimed or an instance closed, at A_UpdateSession, but performs none of those actions itself: the record and the thing it describes are kept deliberately separate.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_ActivityLog/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_ActivityLog",
      "label": "Agent (this session)",
      "scopeNote": "Brackets its own work with a start and an end entry rather than leaving either implied, and reads Gateway_Capture rather than assuming it: persisting when capture is on, but merely reporting the setting — never silently dropping the entry — when it is off or could not be determined.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/activity-log.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_BeanLifecycle/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_BeanLifecycle",
      "label": "Agent (this session)",
      "scopeNote": "Owns every transition on a bean it holds — check, create, claim, work, and the three-way outcome at the end — but GW_Owner is the one branch this lane cannot complete itself: the moment a bean turns out to be someone else's, the only correct move is to leave the whole lifecycle to Lane_Sibling rather than resolve, scrap or edit it from here.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/bean-lifecycle.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CodeChangeReview/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_CodeChangeReview",
      "label": "Authoring agent",
      "scopeNote": "The `no-clean-run-over-an-empty-set` convention is bound at this lane specifically because this is the one lane that writes checks — Lane_Pipeline runs them and Lane_Reviewer reads someone else's, so a check with nothing to assert over is this lane's failure mode to guard against, nobody else's. Every activity that is not mechanical execution (Lane_Pipeline) or an outside judgement (Lane_Reviewer) sits here, including both loop-backs — a red gate returns to Task_Implement through Task_Diagnose, and review findings return to it through Task_AddressReview — so this lane never hands work off without also owning what comes back.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/code-change-review.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeBase/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_MergeBase",
      "label": "Authoring agent",
      "scopeNote": "Reached only when the command refused: an authored conflict, an undeclared path, or a resolution the gates could not reproduce. The refused paths are listed for it; what to do with an authored conflict is judgement.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/merge-base.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeRefusal/Lane_Dispatched",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_MergeRefusal",
      "label": "Dispatched agent",
      "scopeNote": "ONE agent with a modest budget, reached only when no live owner can be. May do what a declared pattern would have done; may NOT decide an authored conflict, which goes to the owner as a question.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/merge-refusal.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_RelatedWork/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_RelatedWork",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Searches, sorts and summarizes, and recommends. It never links, blocks, merges or comments on another piece of work before the user has answered, because coordinating is a commitment on behalf of the work's owners.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/related-work.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_StalledAgentTriage/Lane_Triage",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_StalledAgentTriage",
      "label": "Triage agent",
      "scopeNote": "Reads the footprint the stalled agents left, collects or reconstructs a handover report per agent, groups the work into 2-4 themes, and recommends. It never finishes, closes or deletes another agent's work.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_UpstreamPinWatch/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_UpstreamPinWatch",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Entered only once Lane_Ci has confirmed a pin is behind and filed the issue, never to make that determination itself: A_PickUp's claim is what stops two sessions adopting the same bump. The judgement of adoption is not drawn here either — Call_Adopt hands it to its own reusable process, so this lane is only the hand-off from mechanical detection to judgement, not the judgement itself.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_UpstreamAdoption/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_UpstreamAdoption",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Owns the whole MVP loop end to end except the two calls it cannot make: SF_UA_8 re-enters this lane's own A_Impact on a fixable finding rather than escalating, so a defect gets fixed and re-evidenced here before anyone outside the lane sees it, and Call_OptionsAnalysis sits here specifically because framing the options is not deciding among them — that judgement belongs to PM_Decide in a different lane entirely.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/upstream-version-adoption.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_WireframeDesignReview/Lane_Designer",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_WireframeDesignReview",
      "label": "Designer",
      "scopeNote": "Writes the intent, produces candidates with real content, and runs the mechanical checks. Does not review its own candidates.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/ui/wireframe-design-review.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/onboarding-agent",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Onboarding agent",
      "title": "Onboarding agent",
      "notation": "onboarding-agent",
      "definition": "The authoring agent acting before there is a folio: clarifying what the user means by \"create a folio\", scanning an existing repo, and scaffolding.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
