      "label": "Automated Pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Owns extraction, glossary preparation, injection and round-trip QA — the only machine check for semantic drift — whose findings go to Task_SMEReview whatever they say, so a clean round-trip is evidence for the reviewer, never a bypass of them. The same lane writes the final status.json once sign-off lands, so the official record sits beside the checks that fed it.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/library/human-translation-workflow.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_ActorRoleAdministration/Lane_Audit",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_ActorRoleAdministration",
      "label": "Graph audit (system)",
      "scopeNote": "Runs only after CallActivity_CodeChangeReview has already completed its own review, because the breakage this lane exists to catch — a join across role, lane, actor and skill — is invisible to a code reviewer reading the diff in isolation; ordinary code review clears the edit, and only this lane's whole-graph pass can tell whether it silently broke something three diagrams away.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/actor-role-administration.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_RenderKgToCdn/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_RenderKgToCdn",
      "label": "Build pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Whoever renders: a workflow running the Tool's commands, or an agent running the same ones. A fixed program either way — the judgement about whether to publish was made by the caller before it got here.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/render-kg-to-cdn.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CiHealth/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_CiHealth",
      "label": "Scheduled log sweep",
      "scopeNote": "Named a 'sweep' but every path through it writes something — the report file, the tracking label, and the issue itself (opened, edited or closed) — and keeping all three in one lane is what makes 'one tracking issue, edited in place' enforceable: a write split across lanes would leave two different actors able to touch the same issue with no ordering between them.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/ci-health-watch.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CodeChangeReview/Lane_Pipeline",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_CodeChangeReview",
      "label": "CI/CD pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Exists as a separate lane for one reason: what it tests — the merge of head into base — is not a claim the Agent lane could make about its own tree, so GW_CIGreen has to be fed by an independent run rather than by the agent reporting its own gates as done.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/code-change-review.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CodeQualityGates/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_CodeQualityGates",
      "label": "CI/CD Pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Joins every job before asking anything, then GW_Hard asks specifically about the HARD gates — the two warn-only results reach the same join but never the gate, so this lane's merge/block call is deliberately blind to a red warn-only step it also ran. No count is given here on purpose: this paragraph carried \"seven jobs, five hard\" and then \"six-and-four\", and each was wrong the next time a job was split or folded (beans `om30`, `7fu5`). Count the `# bpmn-node:` lines in the workflow instead.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/code-quality-gates.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_DocsSite/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_DocsSite",
      "label": "CI/CD Pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Before it will even attempt the risky part, GW_Complete can refuse outright and end at End_Refused if a maintained artefact is missing — so an incomplete build never reaches Task_Publish's full replace at all, which is a harder stop than the restore/verify pair further down the same lane makes for a partial one.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/docs-site-publish.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_FeatureStaging/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_FeatureStaging",
      "label": "CI/CD Pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Runs all three entry points — stage, cleanup, cleanup-dispatch — as one actor because none of the work in any of them needs judgement; the one step that does, confirming a dispatch deletion, was carved out into Lane_Human rather than left here. Every path that changes `STAGING/` writes its render-log entry in the SAME commit as the change, because a log push that can fail on its own is exactly how a preview vanishes with nothing on the branch saying why.\n\nA FOURTH trigger starts none of them, and that is deliberate rather than an omission from this diagram. `merge_group` is declared on the workflow so it REPORTS in the merge queue — a required check that never reports on a `merge_group` event leaves every queued pull request pending forever — and all three jobs skip on it. A preview exists for the reviewers of a pull request; a queue entry has none and lives for minutes. Without the skip, `stage`'s existing guards all pass on a queue run (`github.event.action` is empty and the event is not a dispatch), so it would publish `STAGING/&lt;slug&gt;/` named after the ephemeral `gh-readonly-queue/...` ref, and nothing would ever remove it — `Start_Closed` below fires on `pull_request_target: closed`, and a queue branch is never a pull request that closes. That is the `plj1` shape arriving once per MERGE rather than once per pull request.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/feature-staging.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_JsonLdDrift/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_JsonLdDrift",
      "label": "CI/CD Pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "The only lane, running the one task this diagram draws deliberately as a single box rather than five: the five checks it performs are independent of each other and only sequential because one job runs them, so five boxes would assert an ordering that does not exist. Its declared job is also the reason this diagram exists at all — without it, check:workflow-coverage would have nothing here to compare a real job against.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/jsonld-drift-check.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeBase/Lane_Command",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_MergeBase",
      "label": "merge:main command",
      "scopeNote": "Mechanical. Decides nothing a declaration has not decided: a path no pattern names is refused, and the gate set, not this lane, judges the result.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/merge-base.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeTrain/Lane_Pipeline",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_MergeTrain",
      "label": "Build pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Mechanical: merges, regenerates and runs the gates, and reports. Judges nothing a declaration has not decided.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/merge-train.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_PrChecksPresent/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_PrChecksPresent",
      "label": "Scheduled log sweep",
      "scopeNote": "Three exit states, and the job's own colour tracks none of them the way a reader would expect: a finding is fully recorded — issue tracked, PR commented — and the job still ends GREEN, because the finding is the repository's problem to see in the tracking issue, not this lane's to fail on. Only UNKNOWN turns the job itself RED, and one unreadable PR is enough to fail the whole sweep — this lane never reports a partial clean.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/pr-checks-present.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_PublishAlert/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_PublishAlert",
      "label": "CI/CD Pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "The build pipeline, running unattended between the export and the deploy. Raises the one alert, the same way whichever step failed.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/publish-alert.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_PublishVerification/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_PublishVerification",
      "label": "CI/CD Pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Runs every verifier over the exported documents before anything is deployed, and reports pass, fail or could-not-tell. It decides nothing about the release: the caller blocks on anything but a pass.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/publish-verification.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_QaPublish/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_QaPublish",
      "label": "CI/CD Pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Runs both paths as fixed programs. It decides nothing that needs judgement: whether a token can write is read from the event, whether a push was accepted is the push's exit code (never its stderr — spike `3ds9` measured a harmless \"push negotiation failed; proceeding anyway\"), and what retention removes is `planPrune`'s rule. A PR whose state cannot be read is KEPT: could-not-determine never deletes.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/qa-publish.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_RepoHealth/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_RepoHealth",
      "label": "Scheduled log sweep",
      "scopeNote": "The only lane in this diagram, and everything it does is either checking or recording — never removing, which is deletion-requires-confirmation applied to the shape most tempted to break it. It is also where the inversion lives: a real finding leaves the job GREEN and speaks through one tracking issue edited in place, while \"could not tell\" is the only outcome that turns the job RED and leaves that issue deliberately untouched.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/repository-health-watch.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_UpstreamPinWatch/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_UpstreamPinWatch",
      "label": "CI/CD Pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Owns exactly three outcomes and must keep them visibly different: current closes the tracking issue, behind opens or edits it, and UNKNOWN leaves the issue untouched while failing the job anyway — a watchdog that goes blind must never read as clean, so this lane is the one place that distinction cannot be collapsed into a single pass or fail. It hands off at the first sign of judgement: the moment a bump needs adopting, that is Lane_Agent's, never this one's.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_UpstreamAdoption/Lane_Build",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_UpstreamAdoption",
      "label": "CI/CD Pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Produces evidence, not verdicts: Task_Gates going red does not end the process or loop by itself — \"this version breaks us\" is a finding the decider needs to see, not a reason for this lane to stop the run — and Task_Mvp exists so that finding is checked against a real deployed build rather than a description of one.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/sdlc/upstream-version-adoption.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_RenderLog/Lane_Pipeline",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_RenderLog",
      "label": "CI/CD Pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Every branch of GW_What — deploy, takedown, full-replace — is logged by this same lane regardless of which is firing, and the ORDER matters as much as the fact: A_LogRemoved happens before A_Remove specifically so a job that dies mid-step leaves a record of intent rather than an artefact that vanished with nothing said about it.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/ui/staging-render-log.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/board-renderer",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Board renderer",
      "title": "Board renderer",
      "notation": "board-renderer",
      "definition": "Draws a board and performs what the reader has already decided: reads each kind's declared zoom threshold and the layout layer, swaps a card for its avatar, projects an open window onto the canvas, and carries out a confirmed relocation. A system lane — it runs a fixed program and exercises no judgement, which is exactly why every decision in board-open-close.bpmn and board-relocate.bpmn sits in the reader's lane instead. It is NOT the build pipeline: it runs where the reader is, once per request, and publishes nothing.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/validation-pipeline",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Validation pipeline",
      "title": "Validation pipeline",
      "notation": "validation-pipeline",
      "definition": "The mechanical half of the HCI validation gate. Its findings are inputs to the editor's decision, never the decision.",
      "altLabel": [
        "Validation and QA (mechanical + agents)",
        "Verification"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
