      "label": "Publish target",
      "scopeNote": "The one lane whose action makes a URL live, which is exactly why a CDN in front of it is not drawn as a second lane — folding the cache in as a participant would make its URL look like the published one, and the canonical URL is this lane's promise to keep, not the cache's. Uploading and exposing stay two separate moments here rather than one, so a bad layout is still catchable before a reader can reach it.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/kg/kg-to-portal.bpmn"
    },
