      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_CopyOutMaterialized",
      "label": "Source graph — read-only",
      "scopeNote": "This lane holds exactly one task and it WRITES NOTHING, which is the point of drawing it at all. A lane that is only ever read from is the visible form of the rule: the arrow runs out of here and never back. Task_ReadSource is where the process would go wrong if anybody added a step, so its emptiness is load-bearing rather than incidental.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/library/copy-out-materialized.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MaterializeRemote/Lane_2",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/corpus",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_MaterializeRemote",
      "label": "Corpus — L1 source knowledge graph",
      "scopeNote": "Whichever branch Gateway_Gates takes, this lane is where the outcome lands, and it is never silence: Task_Declare and Task_StayRef are the process's only two ends, both bean-noted, because a node with no recorded state is invalid rather than defaulted. A refusal is written down with the same weight as a success — the graph still knows the node exists either way.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/library/materialize-remote.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_RefreshMaterialized/Lane_2",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/corpus",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_RefreshMaterialized",
      "label": "Corpus — L1 source knowledge graph",
      "scopeNote": "Where the refreshed content actually lands, and the one place the five import gates are re-asked rather than inherited — a licence can change since the original import, and a collection can grow past a size somebody already agreed to, so passing the gates once is never treated as passing them for good.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/library/refresh-materialized.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SampleImport/Lane_2",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/corpus",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_SampleImport",
      "label": "Corpus — L1 source knowledge graph",
      "scopeNote": "Every path ends here with something written down. A refused sample stays referenced with the refusing gate's reason, a failed import records what failed, and a passed one records where it landed. None ends in silence, because an import nobody can tell was tried is the one somebody tries again.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/library/sample-import.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SubscribeKg/Lane_2",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/corpus",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_SubscribeKg",
      "label": "Corpus — the subscriber's declaration",
      "scopeNote": "Where the subscription is written down: the entry in the subscriber's instance declaration (choice and pin only, never state), the cached copy of the substrate's declaration the visualizer reads offline, and the record of how the walk ended. A refusal lands here with the same weight as a success, so the next caller does not re-litigate it.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/library/subscribe-kg.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/external-registry",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "External registry",
      "title": "External registry",
      "notation": "external-registry",
      "definition": "Trusted registries and observatories outside this instance's control. Carries no skills because nothing here instructs it.",
      "altLabel": [
        "Portal (external consumer)"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "actedUpon": true,
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_KgToPortal/Lane_Portal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_KgToPortal/Lane_Portal",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/external-registry",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_KgToPortal",
      "label": "Portal (external consumer)",
      "scopeNote": "The only lane outside this instance's control, so P_Verify checks against an external trust anchor — the GDHCN trustlist — rather than against anything the pipeline itself asserts. When that trustlist cannot be reached, this lane's answer is `unknown`, and GW_Verified routes it the same way as a mismatch: to the last good version, never to a guessed pass.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/kg/kg-to-portal.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/log",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Activity log",
      "title": "Activity log",
      "notation": "log",
      "definition": "The agent activity log. A MECHANICAL role and an `actedUpon` one: it is written to at task start and task end, and emptied by an actor — one entry, all of them, or on a periodic sweep — and it decides nothing. Modelled on `work-plan` and `corpus`, the two existing stores that are acted upon rather than acting. Its entries are held in the instance's unpublished store and never reach a published graph; the `activity-log` skill names the location, which is deliberately not repeated here because a role description IS published.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "actedUpon": true
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/session-record",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Session record",
      "title": "Session record",
      "notation": "session-record",
      "definition": "A session's context — who is acting, which instances are open, what it waits on. A MECHANICAL role and an `actedUpon` one: written to as the session moves and read by a sibling deciding whether a claim is live, and it decides nothing. Modelled on `work-plan`, `corpus` and `log`, the stores that are acted upon rather than acting. It carries `session-context` because the shape of what is written IS the discipline here — unlike `work-plan`, whose store has a CLI, this one is written by a machine that may be an LLM playing the part, so the schema is the contract.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "actedUpon": true
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/editorial-authoring-agent",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Editorial authoring agent",
      "title": "Editorial authoring agent",
      "notation": "editorial-authoring-agent",
      "definition": "The authoring agent in the editorial lane: auditing a block's prose, structure and sourcing rather than writing new subject matter.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/docs-authoring-agent",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Docs authoring agent",
      "title": "Docs authoring agent",
      "notation": "docs-authoring-agent",
      "definition": "The authoring agent producing what a person reads ABOUT the instance — generated references, the glossary, sticky notes, theme art and deployment documentation.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-who-iris-site-i18n/cat-harness.jsonld#role/platform-authoring-agent",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Platform authoring agent",
